<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 0.25 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 0.25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 0.19 points, or 0.25 percent, to 76.83 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index provisionally fell 11.69 points to 3,252.31.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 19.71 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
